            "alt": "Refer to caption",
            "desc": "4.2 The concept layer loses physical scale\n\n\nTable 2 reports the concept layer. Without volume supervision,\nthe standard deviation of predicted volumes collapsed to 0.1 mL against\nreference standard deviations of 35.7 and 45.7 mL. The EDV correlation was\n−0.219-0.219; at this predicted spread the correlation is numerically unstable and\nwe treat its sign as uninformative rather than as evidence of anti-correlation.\nThe ESV correlation remained positive at 0.626. The concept layer therefore\nretains part of the ordering while losing the unit, which is precisely the\nbehaviour predicted by Proposition 1. Fig. 1\nshows the effect directly: the ungrounded predictions form a horizontal band near\nzero regardless of the reference volume.\n\n\nFigure 1: Predicted against reference volumes on the test set (n=1,276n=1{,}276).\nTop: without volume supervision the concept layer produces almost\nconstant volumes (predicted SD 0.1 mL against reference SD 35.7 and 45.7 mL;\nacross all 1,276 studies the end-systolic predictions span 0.6–1.4 mL and the\nend-diastolic predictions 1.6–2.0 mL), collapsing onto a narrow band along the\nhorizontal axis; the softplus output\nconstrains that collapse to small positive values rather than to an arbitrary\nconstant. Both rows share axis limits. Bottom: supervision in\nmillilitres restores the spread\n(19.6 and 22.5 mL) and aligns the predictions with the identity line, though the\nremaining slope shows that compression is reduced rather than removed. Dashed\nline is identity.\n\n\nTable 2: Concept Layer Grounding on the Test Set (n=1,276n=1{,}276). Predicted SD Is the Quantity of Interest for Scale.\n\n\n\n\nEnd-systolic volume\nEnd-diastolic volume\n\n\nCondition\nMAE (mL)\nrr\npred. SD\nMAE (mL)\nrr\npred. SD\n\n\nReference\n—\n—\n35.7\n—\n—\n45.7\n\n\nCBM, EF only\n42.96\n0.626\n0.1\n89.79\n−0.219-0.219\n0.1\n\n\nCBM, grounded μ=3\\mu=3\n\n16.03\n0.663\n19.6\n25.83\n0.569\n22.5\n\n\nCBM, normalized\n16.59\n0.600\n18.1\n26.50\n0.523\n21.5\n\n\nCBM, grounded μ=10\\mu=10\n\n16.60\n0.623\n17.9\n26.50\n0.547\n22.5",
